# Overview {#sec-panorama}

Before exploring the results, it is important to understand the **scale** of the analysis. The corpus combines hundreds of articles processed through AI-assisted coding, producing a knowledge network with thousands of causal relations.

::: {#cell-panorama-stats .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
overview = pd.DataFrame([
    {"Metric": "Articles analyzed", "Value": stats.source_count,
     "What it means": "Scientific sources processed by the pipeline"},
    {"Metric": "Evidence extracted", "Value": stats.item_count,
     "What it means": "Excerpts with identified causal chains"},
    {"Metric": "Concepts in the ontology", "Value": stats.ontology_count,
     "What it means": "Unique factors classified along several dimensions"},
    {"Metric": "Causal relations", "Value": stats.triple_count,
     "What it means": "A → relation → B connections between concepts"},
])

display(overview.style.hide(axis='index').set_properties(**{
    'text-align': 'left'
}).set_table_styles([
    {'selector': 'th', 'props': [('text-align', 'left'), ('font-weight', 'bold')]}
]))
```

