# Central Concepts {#sec-conceitos}

The concepts that appear with the highest **frequency** and across the greatest **diversity of sources** are the most empirically evident. If many independent articles identify the same factor, it is probably central to the field.

::: {#cell-fig-top-concepts .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
top25 = concept_stats.head(25).reset_index()

fig = px.bar(
    top25.iloc[::-1],
    x="frequency", y="concept",
    color="sources",
    color_continuous_scale="YlOrRd",
    orientation="h",
    labels={"concept": "", "frequency": "Occurrences in causal chains",
            "sources": "Sources"},
    height=600,
)
fig.update_layout(
    template="plotly_white",
    font=dict(size=12),
    coloraxis_colorbar=dict(title="No. of<br>sources"),
)
fig.show()
```

