# Types of Causal Relation {#sec-relacoes}

The template defines five relation types. Their distribution reveals the **nature** of the field: whether factors predominantly *enable*, *influence*, *constrain* or *contest* one another.

::: {#fig-relation-types .cell execution_count=4}
``` {.python .cell-code}
rel_counts = chains["relation"].value_counts().reset_index()
rel_counts.columns = ["Relation type", "Count"]

rel_descriptions = {
    "INFLUENCES": "Direct causal effect (A affects B)",
    "ENABLES": "Facilitating condition (A allows B)",
    "CONSTRAINS": "Restriction (A limits B)",
    "RELATES-TO": "Generic association",
    "CONTESTED-BY": "Active opposition (A is contested by B)",
}
rel_counts["Meaning"] = rel_counts["Relation type"].map(rel_descriptions)

fig = px.pie(
    rel_counts,
    values="Count", names="Relation type",
    color_discrete_sequence=px.colors.qualitative.Set2,
    hole=0.4,
)
fig.update_traces(textposition="inside", textinfo="percent+label+value")
fig.update_layout(template="plotly_white", font=dict(size=12))
fig.show()

display(rel_counts.style.hide(axis='index'))
```

