# Most Documented Relations {#sec-top-relacoes}

Each `A → type → B` relation expresses a causal hypothesis extracted from the literature. The most frequent relations represent the **most widely documented mechanisms**.

::: {#cell-fig-top-relations .cell execution_count=5}
``` {.python .cell-code}
rel_freq = (
    chains.groupby(["from_code", "relation", "to_code"])
    .agg(occurrences=("bibref", "count"), sources=("bibref", "nunique"))
    .sort_values("occurrences", ascending=False)
    .reset_index()
)

top20_rel = rel_freq.head(20).copy()
top20_rel["chain_label"] = (
    top20_rel["from_code"] + " → " +
    top20_rel["relation"].str.lower() + " → " +
    top20_rel["to_code"]
)

fig = px.bar(
    top20_rel.iloc[::-1],
    x="occurrences", y="chain_label",
    color="relation",
    orientation="h",
    labels={"chain_label": "", "occurrences": "Occurrences", "relation": "Type"},
    color_discrete_map={
        "INFLUENCES": "#4CAF50", "ENABLES": "#2196F3",
        "CONSTRAINS": "#FF9800", "CONTESTED-BY": "#F44336",
        "RELATES-TO": "#9E9E9E",
    },
    height=600,
)
fig.update_layout(template="plotly_white", font=dict(size=11))
fig.show()
```

