# Dooyeweerd's Modal Aspects {#sec-dooyeweerd}

Dooyeweerd's modal classification organizes concepts into **16 aspects** running from the quantitative to the fiducial. The distribution reveals which dimensions of reality are most studied --- and which are neglected.

::: {#fig-aspects .cell execution_count=6}
``` {.python .cell-code}
aspect_counts = onto["aspect"].value_counts().sort_index()
aspect_df = pd.DataFrame({
    "aspect_id": aspect_counts.index,
    "count": aspect_counts.values,
})
aspect_df["label"] = aspect_df["aspect_id"].map(aspect_labels)
aspect_df["order"] = aspect_df["aspect_id"].astype(int)
aspect_df = aspect_df.sort_values("order")

aspect_df["group"] = aspect_df["order"].apply(
    lambda x: "Pre-analytical (1-6)" if x <= 6 else "Normative (7-15)" if x >= 7 else "N/A"
)

fig = px.bar(
    aspect_df[aspect_df["order"] > 0],
    x="label", y="count",
    color="group",
    labels={"label": "Modal aspect", "count": "No. of concepts", "group": ""},
    color_discrete_map={
        "Pre-analytical (1-6)": "#42A5F5",
        "Normative (7-15)": "#AB47BC",
    },
    height=450,
)
fig.update_layout(
    template="plotly_white",
    xaxis_tickangle=-45,
    font=dict(size=12),
    bargap=0.15,
)
fig.show()

top3 = aspect_df[aspect_df["order"] > 0].nlargest(3, "count")
display(Markdown(
    f"**Dominant aspects:** {', '.join(top3['label'])} — "
    f"together they account for {top3['count'].sum()} of {aspect_df['count'].sum()} concepts "
    f"({top3['count'].sum()/aspect_df['count'].sum()*100:.0f}%)."
))
```

