# Robustness of Concepts {#sec-confianca}

Each concept receives a confidence level based on frequency and source diversity. **HIGH** concepts appear in many articles; **LOW** concepts emerge from few sources.

::: {#fig-confidence .cell execution_count=8}
``` {.python .cell-code}
conf_counts = onto["confidence"].value_counts().reindex(["HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]).reset_index()
conf_counts.columns = ["Level", "Concepts"]

fig = px.bar(
    conf_counts,
    x="Level", y="Concepts",
    color="Level",
    color_discrete_map={"HIGH": "#2E7D32", "MEDIUM": "#F9A825", "LOW": "#C62828"},
    text="Concepts",
    height=400,
)
fig.update_traces(textposition="outside")
fig.update_layout(template="plotly_white", showlegend=False, font=dict(size=13))
fig.show()

pct_low = conf_counts[conf_counts["Level"] == "LOW"]["Concepts"].values[0] / conf_counts["Concepts"].sum() * 100
display(Markdown(
    f"**{pct_low:.0f}%** of the concepts have LOW confidence — typical of a broad corpus where "
    f"many concepts are specific to a few studies. The {conf_counts[conf_counts['Level']=='HIGH']['Concepts'].values[0]} "
    f"HIGH concepts form the consolidated core of the field."
))
